WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.753
In this video, we are going to properly
 set up and use a balance together.

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:06.965
Before using a balance, you want to make
 sure it's properly calibrated.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:10.969
The way that you calibrate a balance
 is with pre calibrated weight standards.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:12.053
They look like this. 

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:14.931
Now you want to make sure that the balance
 has been plugged in for

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:19.019
about an hour or two before you start,
 the next step is to level the balance.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.730
You do that by turning the dials
 on the sides of the balance

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.314
to make sure that the bubble
 is in the center. 

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.025
Now it's time to calibrate. 

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.235
Normally
 there's a 'Cal' button on the balance.

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:31.364
Some balances have internal cal,
 and that's fine for daily calibration.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:36.036
For more thorough calibration,
 we want to do a spanning cal from here.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:39.330
The balance will prompt you to place
 pre calibrated weight standards.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.876
Place the weights when prompted
 and store the values when you're done.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.627
You can now use the balance 

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:48.548
when there's nothing on the balance,
 you use '0' to zero everything out.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.966
'Tare' is not zero. 

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.802
Tare is only used
 when something is on the balance

00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:54.554
and you want to remove the weight of that
 something. 

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.974
Use tare when you want to weigh
 something in something.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.810
Pretty simplistic, but you'd be surprised
 how many people get that wrong.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:01.561
There you have it. 

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.272
That's how you set up
 and properly use a balance.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:08.109
If you want us to keep making more videos
 to help make your life in the lab easier.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.194
Like and subscribe.

